    "<a href='https://metadata.cacore.ca/Details/id=612' rel='nofollow ugc' target='_blank'>Click here</a> for metadata. An Issues Contributing Area (ICA) is an area within a vulnerable area where activities could contribute to a water quality issue. For the Village of Madoc wells this area is a 30 metre setback from a watercourse or wetland within the WHPA E or F. There are no other Issues Contributing Areas identified in the Quinte Region."
